// TEST: Anon Range Flat Elementwise
// The anonymous range reaches the FLAT ELEMENTWISE path (docs/plan-cpp-perf-
// exploitation.md phase 3), exactly as the named `range<I>` spelling does.
//
// It did not always. The range carries the reserved tag `__anon`, and both
// halves of the flat gate (CodeGenLoopNest's `flatShapeSignature` and its
// element-level twin) refused any `__`-prefixed tag outright. Every OTHER
// reserved tag also carries a non-plain IxKind and was already refused on that
// ground, so `__anon` -- a plain contiguous skeleton -- was the only thing the
// blanket prefix test actually excluded. The cost was invisible in values and
// real in code: `x0 + dx * Float64(0..n)`, the idiom CLAUDE.md names the top
// rung of the ladder, emitted a nest with no BLADE_RESTRICT pool pointers and
// no BLADE_IVDEP, while the identical `Float64(range<I>)` got both. The gate
// now names `__halowin` (whose reads are OFFSET from the loop index, so its
// flat index really is not the operand's pool offset) and nothing else.
//
// `t * t` puts one array in both operand positions, which is also the flat
// emitter's pool-dedup case: two ArrayPositions, one pointer declaration.
// `sqrt` over perfect squares keeps the pins exact -- and is the same loop
// shape `-fno-math-errno` (src/Build.fs) exists to let g++ vectorize.
// Extent 7 is non-power-of-two, per the repo's stride discipline.
let axis = 1.5 + 0.25 * Float64(0..7)
let t = Float64(0..7)
let squares = t * t
let roots = sqrt(squares)
// EXPECT: axis = [1.5, 1.75, 2, 2.25, 2.5, 2.75, 3]
// EXPECT: squares = [0, 1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36]
// EXPECT: roots = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
